s", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn8le08ob05re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le08ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn8le08ob05re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100 ", "image": "engenn8le08ob05re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Where can Rosa be? She told me she would meet me here at 7, and it's already 7:30. We could lose the beginning of the baseball game if she is too late. She might be stuck in traffic, who knows? I'm sure that she must have a good reason for not being on time. I can't stand it when people aren't punctual!"}, {"time": "20000", "image": "engenn8le08ob05re2img05.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Rosa</span>:\t\tPeter! Nice to see you!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tHi Rosa, I'm happy to finally see you, too.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Rosa</span>:\t\tWhat's wrong? You sound upset.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tIt's nothing \u2026 Well, it's just that I had bought these tickets for the game before we decided to meet in this restaurant. We may not make it for the beginning now."}, {"time": "38000", "image": "engenn8le08ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Rosa</span>:\t\tOh, I'm sorry, Peter. I must have lost track of the time. I had thought about setting up my alarm, but I forgot. I usually don't look at my watch, either.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tSo, the stereotypes about Italians are true?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Rosa</span>:\t\tYou may be right. I hadn't noticed how we Italians cut in line all the time until I came to the States. We're not very good at queuing up, I guess.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tI suppose you could make an effort."}, {"time": "65000", "image": "engenn8le08ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 4, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Rosa</span>:\t\tWe're too busy being affectionate for that!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tThat's true, even though some people here may think that you're too touchy-feely.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Rosa</span>:\t\tMaybe we could order something now, what do you think?"}]}}], "_data": [], "id": 1, "type": "audio"}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "p", "value": "<span class=\"strong\">Andy</span>: I had never thought about national stereotypes. But now that we are friends I have noticed a couple of interesting things.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Friend</span>: It\u00b4s true. We, for example, are not really punctual. I think it must be because we don't really pay attention to the time.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Andy</span>: I hope you can make an effort to avoid that. People here are really touchy regarding punctuality. \n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Friend</span>: I know! Also, you have a big issue with not queuing. It might be related to the way you work over here.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Andy</span>: Do you think so?"}], "_data": [], "id": 2, "type": "text"}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter's Dating Misadventures", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Waiting at the Restaurant", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "  Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Simple Past vs Past Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Perfect tense to identify and talk about an 'earlier past'.<br />You use the Simple Past to talk about a finished action that happened at a specific time in the past. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " When you are talking about a past event, you can refer to something that happened at an earlier time to that past event by using the <span class=\"underline\">Past Perfect</span> tense.<br /><br />  The structure of the Past Perfect is:<br /><br />  Subject + had + past participle<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had thought</span> about setting up my alarm, but I forgot</span>.<br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">first</span>? I thought about setting up the alarm.<br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">later</span>? I forgot.<br /><br />  You use the Past Perfect tense (not Simple Past) when you want to talk about how long something had continued <span class=\"strong\">up to a past moment</span>. <br /> Example:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">I hadn't noticed how we Italians cut in line all the time until I came to the States</span>. <br /><br />  You use the Simple Past tense to talk about the action that happened after that prior action in the Past Perfect tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I had bought these tickets for the game before we decided to meet in this restaurant. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modals for Possibility and Certainty ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.<br /> You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> may</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span>  to describe degrees of certainty.<br /> You can use modals with the Present Perfect to talk about the possibility of a past event that is not clear in the present context.<br /> Example:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">must have </span> lost track of the time.</span><br /><br />   Must = it's very likely <br /> Must not / Could not / Can't = it's not possible<br /> May / Might / Can / Could = it's possible<br /> May not / Might not = it's possible this is not true", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Modal </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Meaning </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> She must have a good reason for not being on time. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's very likely she has a good reason.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I can't stand it when people aren't punctual! </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It is not possible for me to accept.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> We could miss the beginning of the baseball game. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible to miss the beginning.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> We may not make it for the beginning now. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's not likely that we can make it for the beginning.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "punctual ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " used to describe a person who is always on time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't stand it when people aren't punctual!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in social situations", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lose track  of", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to fail to keep informed or aware of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I must have lost track of the time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to queue up", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to form a line; to stand in line", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We're not very good at queuing up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cut (in line)", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to enter a line without queuing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hadn't noticed how we Italians cut in line all the time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "affectionate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to describe a person who easily reveals their feelings or emotions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We're too busy being affectionate for that!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "touchy-feely", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to describe a person who openly displays their emotions and affections", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some people here may think that you're too touchy-feely.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On a blank piece of paper, create a timeline of your life.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include all of the most important events (e.g. moves, graduations, jobs, vacations).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen as your partner presents their timeline, ask at least five follow-up questions (e.g. \u201cHad you ever been to Cuba before?\u201d).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your timeline and answer your partner's follow-up questions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I create a timeline of past events", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present a past narrative", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask questions about the past", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I respond to questions about the past", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}